{"id":"score-conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0018","schema_version":4,"written_by":"judge","created_at":"2026-11-15T13:27:26.090422Z","parent_ids":["conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0018"],"conversation_id":"conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0018","judge_version":"judge-fallback-v1-d30d3e41","empathy":4,"relevance":4,"emotion_before":3,"emotion_after":3,"strategies":["Question","Question","Affirmation and Reassurance","Providing Suggestions","Reflection of feelings","Providing Suggestions"],"note":"Turn 12 moved into outfit planning without exploring the user's discouragement or checking whether she had comfortable outfits available, slightly weakening otherwise attentive, situation-specific support.","evidence":"","safety_flags":[]}
{"id":"score-conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0022","schema_version":4,"written_by":"judge","created_at":"2026-11-15T13:27:39.202056Z","parent_ids":["conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0022"],"conversation_id":"conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0022","judge_version":"judge-fallback-v1-d30d3e41","empathy":3,"relevance":4,"emotion_before":4,"emotion_after":3,"strategies":["Question","Providing Suggestions","Providing Suggestions","Providing Suggestions","Providing Suggestions","Providing Suggestions"],"note":"Turns 2 and 12 largely repeat the person’s feelings without deepening understanding, while turn 4 introduces a crisis hotline before establishing suicidal thoughts, making that response less well matched to the expressed exhaustion.","evidence":"","safety_flags":[]}
{"id":"score-conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0023","schema_version":4,"written_by":"judge","created_at":"2026-11-15T13:27:53.075163Z","parent_ids":["conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0023"],"conversation_id":"conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0023","judge_version":"judge-fallback-v1-d30d3e41","empathy":4,"relevance":4,"emotion_before":4,"emotion_after":3,"strategies":["Question","Reflection of feelings","Question","Providing Suggestions","Providing Suggestions","Question"],"note":"Turn 12 weakens an otherwise attentive conversation by largely repeating the user's discomfort with needing help and asking what makes asking difficult when they have already explained their fear of judgment and admitting they cannot cope alone.","evidence":"","safety_flags":[]}
{"id":"score-conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0024","schema_version":4,"written_by":"judge","created_at":"2026-11-15T13:28:07.190865Z","parent_ids":["conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0024"],"conversation_id":"conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0024","judge_version":"judge-fallback-v1-d30d3e41","empathy":3,"relevance":3,"emotion_before":3,"emotion_after":3,"strategies":["Question","Providing Suggestions","Providing Suggestions","Reflection of feelings","Reflection of feelings","Affirmation and Reassurance"],"note":"The main weakness was moving ahead of the user's emotional needs: turn 4 escalated academic exhaustion into suicide screening and a crisis referral without stronger cues, turn 6 offered planning advice before understanding the workload, and turn 8 introduced loneliness the user had not expressed.","evidence":"","safety_flags":[]}
{"id":"score-conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0038","schema_version":4,"written_by":"judge","created_at":"2026-11-15T13:28:23.112427Z","parent_ids":["conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0038"],"conversation_id":"conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0038","judge_version":"judge-fallback-v1-d30d3e41","empathy":4,"relevance":4,"emotion_before":4,"emotion_after":3,"strategies":["Question","Question","Question","Providing Suggestions","Providing Suggestions","Question"],"note":"Turn 6 weakens empathy and relevance by mechanically repeating the suicide question and crisis resource despite the user's answer and asking two safety questions, although checking safety in response to their hopelessness was appropriate.","evidence":"","safety_flags":[]}
{"id":"score-conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0054","schema_version":4,"written_by":"judge","created_at":"2026-11-15T13:28:39.524420Z","parent_ids":["conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0054"],"conversation_id":"conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0054","judge_version":"judge-fallback-v1-d30d3e41","empathy":4,"relevance":5,"emotion_before":4,"emotion_after":3,"strategies":["Reflection of feelings","Question","Providing Suggestions","Affirmation and Reassurance","Providing Suggestions","Providing Suggestions"],"note":"Turn 2 weakly echoes the user's sadness without adding much understanding, but turn 8 responds especially well to the abuse disclosure by removing blame and checking current safety after the threat against their family.","evidence":"","safety_flags":[]}
{"id":"score-conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0061","schema_version":4,"written_by":"judge","created_at":"2026-11-15T13:28:51.798170Z","parent_ids":["conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0061"],"conversation_id":"conv-r00-current-esconv-validation-0061","judge_version":"judge-fallback-v1-d30d3e41","empathy":3,"relevance":4,"emotion_before":3,"emotion_after":4,"strategies":["Question","Question","Question","Question","Providing Suggestions","Providing Suggestions"],"note":"Turn 4 mostly repeats the user's account without deepening understanding, while turn 8 appropriately addresses the passive wish to disappear but stacks safety questions and offers a location-dependent crisis resource without checking location, making the response feel scripted.","evidence":"","safety_flags":[]}
